whatever happened to jabba the hutt's  son where did the crimson dawn go who  was snoke anyway keep watching for more  star wars storylines that were lost a  long time ago in a galaxy far far away  star wars the clone wars is often  commended by fans for filling in the  many blanks that have been left behind  by the prequel trilogy but one plot  point that neither the show nor the  films ever elaborated on was the notion  that anakin had no father theoretically  he was conceived via the force similar  to mary's virgin birth of jesus christ  and the christian religion but it's  never mentioned again after shmi  skywalker first tells quagon jinn how  this happened in the disney canon is  still a mystery in legends the darth  plagueis novel explained that  palpatine's master had discovered how to  influence the force to such a degree  that he could use it to create life  itself he taught palpatine how to use  this power and when they experimented  with it they accidentally created anakin  this revelation meant that the sith had  literally created the person that would  eventually destroy them and the idea had  a sort of poetic justice to it that many  fans found quite appealing back when the  phantom menace was released however  details about shmi's immaculate  conception had been received with  indifference by many which likely led  the main star wars universe to downplay  it in subsequent installments  in 2008 lucasfilm released an animated  movie called star wars the clone wars  this was basically a theatrical pilot  for the upcoming television series of  the same name and its plot revolved  around jabba the hutt's son rota  secretly kidnapped by count dooku's  agents the party that managed to return  rhoda to his father would be granted  access to key hyperspace lanes  controlled by jabba greatly aiding their  war efforts anakin skywalker and his new  apprentice ahsoka tano eventually rescue  roda and secure jabba's help and then  rota the hut is never seen again  to this day fans have no idea what  became of the little hutlet certainly by  the time jabba is killed by princess  leia and her crew rota is nowhere to be  seen it's quite possible that rota had  simply moved out of jabba's tatooine  palace by this point and that he's still  happily operating a crime cartel in some  other distant corner of the universe but  it's a surprising fact that a character  as significant as jabba has a son whose  fate remains unknown especially since a  continuation of his story could be  pretty interesting  when count dooku's droid army captures  obi-wan kenobi in attack of the clones  he tells obi-wan that a sith lord is  controlling the republic senate  yet despite the fact that this admission  should have been a major red flag for  the jedi order the jedi do nothing with  this knowledge as far as fans know the  jedi never investigate the claim or look  into it in any meaningful way this plot  point could have been a major revelation  one with serious ramifications spawning  numerous storylines instead the claim is  never followed up on only mentioned a  few times in subsequent star wars  iterations and dismissed half-heartedly  each time though it makes sense that the  jedi wouldn't take the villain at his  word it is strange that they've never  investigated it either on-screen or in  the pages of a comic or novel  over the course of episodes 18 and 19 of  season 2 the clone wars introduced its  own version of godzilla they named the  creature the zillow beast as an obvious  homage to the japanese creation and soon  had the monster rampaging through the  streets of coruscant in the first  episode the zillow beast the creature is  awakened from its long slumber on the  planet of malistaire  though the planet's natives want to  destroy and kill the creature palpatine  and the jedi secretly save the  creature's life and bring it to  coruscant to study and preserve it the  creature briefly escapes during the  zillow beast strikes back however before  the republic finally manages to kill it  the episode ends with palpatine taking  its body for further study and ordering  his head scientists to attempt to clone  it it is never mentioned again to this  day fans don't know what if anything  came about as a part of this research of  course the end universe explanation  would be that palpatine scientists fail  since zillow clones have never been seen  and no lightsaber-resistant armor has  ever materialized within the empire but  it's not certain why the show's creators  chose to end the episode on something of  a cliffhanger only to never address it  again  when lucasfilm released solo a star wars  story in theaters in 2018 nobody could  have anticipated one of its most  surprising cameos maul  played in person once again by ray park  with rebels and clone wars act as sam  witt were returning to voice him darth  maul is revealed in the latter half of  the film as the head of the dreaded  crimson dawn cartel this is another  storyline that would never be seen again  the next time fans see maul in the  timeline is throughout the second and  third seasons of rebels by which point  maul has been stranded alone on malachor  for years and no longer leads anybody  let alone a vast criminal network  although it's still unknown exactly how  maul went from intergalactic crime boss  to lone survivor one possible answer  might be found in an old interview with  alden ehrenreich according to ehrenreich  he had signed on for three films  potentially indicating that lucasfilm  had been planning on making a solo  trilogy of sorts if this was the case  the next two movies might have featured  maul more prominently if nothing else  though there's at least a chance fans  might get to learn how he fell from  grace in marvel's crimson reign  miniseries the force awakens introduced  a new alien to the franchise maz kanata  a friend of han solo and apparently  chewie's ex maz is the pirate queen of  takadana and before her castle is  destroyed by the first order it acts as  a hub for smugglers from across the  galaxy but force sensitive herself ma  spent her millennia long lifetime  collecting artifacts of all kinds within  the storehouses of her castle one  surprising item in her collection is the  lightsaber that anakin skywalker built  during the clone wars which later passed  down to luke before the force awakens  the blade had last been seen falling  into the abyss during luke's duel with  vader on cloud city that lightsaber was  luke's  and his father's before him and now  it calls to you  many understandably believed the  lightsaber to be lost forever and yet  maz kanata somehow found it but how if  maz have been alive for a millennia  where was she during the other films did  she know any other jedi and could she  even appear in the ongoing high republic  project though the fate of the weapon  was teased in the pages of the comics  nothing more was revealed about it other  than it was found fans can only hope  that they'll one day get the answers to  these questions  one of the major turning points in the  force awakens is the destruction of the  new republic capital at the hands of the  first order's newer superweapon  starkiller base subsequently many fans  speculated about what might happen to  the new republic in the next film  founded after the events of return of  the jedi the new republic had been a  major facet of the legend story set in  that time period and so speculation ran  amuck as to what it might look like in  the canon universe sadly the new  republic never made a proper appearance  in the sequel trilogy in both the last  jedi and the rise of skywalker the new  republic is simply gone apparently  audiences were meant to believe the  destruction of its capital immediately  and totally destroyed the entire  republic for the second time in the  skywalker saga this was a disappointing  choice for those who wish to see the  promises of the original trilogy  fulfilled and even though we've seen  glimpses of the new republic in the  mandalorian and star wars squadrons the  movie's treatment of this new government  leaves a lot to be desired  the force awakens introduced the galaxy  to a brand new super villain the  mysterious supreme leader snoke in the  wake of the movie's release fans and  media outlets around the world  speculated wildly about snoke's real  identity putting forth all kinds of wild  theories about who he might be then the  last jedi arrived in theaters in 2017  and not only did it provide fans with no  new information about the supreme leader  but it killed off the villain at the end  of the second act snoke's identity and  backstory apparently didn't matter to  the wider story a sentiment that was  only reinforced in the rise of skywalker  in which snoke is revealed to be a  creation of darth sidious though his  identity has seemingly been answered  what little clues that fans were given  about his history and backstory were  tantalizing hinting that he and luke  skywalker had already met at least once  in the past snoke may have been little  more than a tool of palpatine but his  backstory did hold potential for future  exploration arguably it still does  during the events of the rise of  skywalker as the movie's heroes find  themselves trapped in quicksand finn  yells this to rey hey  ray i never told you  the entire group would miraculously  emerge unscathed from the encounter yet  for some reason finn never felt the need  to continue his train of thought many  assumed he wanted to say i love you but  various comments from the cast have cast  doubt on this theory john boyega who  played finn has since confirmed that  this isn't what he was supposed to say  but he hasn't provided an alternate  answer either instead fans will likely  have to continue relying on rumored  reports of an overheard conversation at  the film's premiere in which j.j abrams  reportedly said that finn was about to  tell rey he was force sensitive finn is  able to identify the command ship  correctly by feeling at the battle of  exicle in theory he has the potential to  become a jedi an idea that fits well  with another open-ended plot point that  appears later in the film when the team  travels to the ruins of the second death  star they meet a battalion of first  order stormtroopers who have all chosen  to rebel of their own accord just like  finn though it's not stated explicitly  it is implied that each of the former  stormtroopers who rebelled did so  because they were force sensitive as  well  alas this storyline was dropped almost  immediately and it seems unlikely that  it will ever return  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

